{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghc4RwqvE3F3xCPt6oTa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bivs3MpqUHZUjCBXf7Hyva","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-8idoi_b1/NOTES.md","content":"# Parity of x[1], x[5], x[9], x[14]\n\nLet s = x1 + x5 + x9 + x14 (integer 0..4). Parity(s) is the piecewise-linear \"zigzag\"\nf(s) = s - 2·relu(s-1) + 2·relu(s-2) - 2·relu(s-3), giving 0,1,0,1,0 for s = 0..4.\n\n- **Layer 1**: units 0..3 compute relu(s - k) for k = 0,1,2,3 (weight 1 on the four tapped bits, bias -k). Distractor bits get zero weight.\n- **Layer 2**: unit 0 combines them with weights (1, -2, 2, -2), so it outputs exactly the parity (0 or 1); the relu does nothing since f ≥ 0.\n- **Output**: logit1 = p, logit0 = 0.5, so argmax gives class 1 exactly when parity is odd.\n\nAll other units are zero. The computation is exact on binary inputs, so accuracy is 100%.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":5340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d702f53-e4bd-47b0-93ee-b6d0bb493e4d","uuid":"056cbdd8-d277-41ab-8228-fd16b17b8ab6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:53:32.591Z","request_id":"req_011Cghc4Rc1VyPDCPhnKm9zG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Bivs3MpqUHZUjCBXf7Hyva":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-8idoi_b1/NOTES.md","content":"# Parity of x[1], x[5], x[9], x[14]\n\nLet s = x1 + x5 + x9 + x14 (integer 0..4). Parity(s) is the piecewise-linear \"zigzag\"\nf(s) = s - 2·relu(s-1) + 2·relu(s-2) - 2·re